<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_PoisonForestFauna.xml            SUUSH_CAULDRON_DRIFTER_1, new 2026-09-26

  The Suush — owner's ask, verbatim (infrastructure/state/items/
  SUUSH_CAULDRON_DRIFTER_1.md): "an Aerofleet-like creature ... that floats
  around the Cauldron feasting on the strange chemistry of its roiling
  atmosphere and that detonates when you shoot it ... a floating spherical
  entity with hanging 'gathering tentacles' like a jellyfish. Make it both
  disturbing and beautiful. Size 2 cells. Docile, tamable, bizarre."

  Grounding, per the item's own research: the real AA_Aerofleet (already
  resident in this biome's own wildAnimals list below) floats via Vanilla
  Expanded Framework's class-side CompFloating — a donor dependency. This
  build takes the item's own steer ("prefer our own floating comp over
  taking a new dependency for a brand-new creature") and goes one further:
  it uses CORE 1.6's own native flight system (CLAUDE.md "If it flies in the
  fiction, it flies in the game" / MaxFlightTime+FlightCooldown+race flags —
  the SAME mechanism vanilla's Chicken/Duck/Goose/Sparrow already use, MEASURED
  against the decompiled engine this pass) rather than either a donor comp OR
  new bespoke C#. No new class was written for flight.

  MECHANISM 1 — floats continuously, not the ground-walk-then-occasional-
  flight of a normal flyer:
    - <MaxFlightTime>600</MaxFlightTime> (statBases, seconds): flight lasts
      10 real-world minutes before a forced landing, effectively "always
      airborne" at normal play timescales.
    - <FlightCooldown>1</FlightCooldown>: if it ever does land, it can take
      off again almost immediately.
    - <flightStartChanceOnJobStart>1.0</flightStartChanceOnJobStart>: it
      rolls to fly at EVERY job start (Pawn_FlightTracker.Notify_JobStarted,
      MEASURED from RimWorld/Pawn_FlightTracker.cs) — combined with the above,
      it reads as continuously drifting rather than a bird that occasionally
      takes wing.
    - <canFlyIntoMap>true</canFlyIntoMap>: arrives already floating.
    - <canLeaveMapFlying>false</canLeaveMapFlying>: it is a Cauldron resident,
      not a migrating bird — it does not fly itself off the map.
    - <body>Bird</body>: reusing vanilla's own bird body (rather than
      inventing one, or borrowing the Anomaly Nociosphere body, which is built
      for a doesntMove=true stationary entity and risks losing the "Moving"
      capacity entirely) — this is the exact body type Chicken/Duck/Goose
      already prove compatible with these same flight fields. The body is
      never rendered (art is the full custom sprite below), so its "wings"
      internally cost nothing visually on a limbless jellyfish silhouette.

  MECHANISM 2 — feeds on the atmosphere, not on plants (the item's own
  explicit "not VegetarianRoughAnimal" steer):
    - <foodType>None</foodType>. RaceProperties.EatsFood => foodType !=
      FoodTypeFlags.None (MEASURED, Verse/RaceProperties.cs:293) — with
      foodType None the Suush never gets a Food need at all: no hunger, no
      foraging, no colonist ever has to feed it. This is the existing vanilla
      pattern the item asked for ("whatever food route expresses 'grazes the
      air' ... don't invent a whole new atmosphere-feeding system") rather
      than a bespoke gas-metabolism mechanic. It also means WorkGiver_Tame's
      "bring food first" gate (which checks RaceProps.EatsFood) is skipped —
      taming it needs no bait, matching "it eats the air, not anything you
      carry."

  MECHANISM 3 — detonates when SHOT, not merely when killed (the item's own
  distinction: "he said shot, not killed ... CompExplosive's territory"):
    - CompProperties_Explosive (vanilla core, no new C#) with
      startWickOnDamageTaken listing Bullet and Bomb — ranged gunfire and
      explosive damage starts the fuse immediately, before the creature is
      anywhere near dead, which is the "nastier" reading the item asked for.
      Melee damage (Cut/Stab/Blunt/Bite/Scratch) does NOT trigger this path.
    - explodeOnKilled is ALSO set true as a backstop: however it actually
      dies, it goes up (CompExplosive.PostDestroy, DestroyMode.KillFinalize —
      MEASURED, fires generically for Pawns same as any ThingWithComps).
    - postExplosionGasType ToxGas: what actually detonates is the roiling
      chemistry it has been gorging on all along — ties the explosion back
      to mechanism 2's fiction rather than being a generic bomb.
    - Default startWickHitPointsPercent (0.2) is left in place as a second,
      redundant trigger; Thing.HitPoints tracking on a Pawn is not guaranteed
      to reflect body-part health the same way a building's does, so the
      dinfo.Def match above is the mechanism actually relied on, not this
      fallback.

  TAMING — verified against the engine, not assumed (item's own instruction):
    TameUtility.CanTame (RimWorld/TameUtility.cs, MEASURED) gates on
    RaceProps.Animal + Faction null + StatDefOf.Wildness < 1 + not a Dryad +
    no Scaria. It does NOT read RaceProps.trainability at all.
    Pawn_TrainingTracker.CanAssignToTrain (MEASURED) confirms trainability
    only gates TRICK training (Obedience etc.) — Tameness training itself has
    no trainability requirement, which is how vanilla's own trainability:None
    animals (turkeys) are tameable. So the Suush keeps trainability None
    (matching the Aerofleet precedent, and fitting "mindless drifting
    gasbag") while Wildness 0.5 (statBases) keeps it genuinely, moderately
    tameable — bizarre wildlife, not a starting pet.

  DOCILE: predator false, manhunterOnDamageChance 0, manhunterOnTameFailChance
  0, no <tools> at all (it has no attack verbs whatsoever) — "the least
  threatening thing on the map" per the item's own framing.

  CAST: solitary (wildGroupSize 1, herdAnimal false) — a single drifting
  oddity, not a herd; this build's own judgment call, not an owner ruling,
  and reversible without ceremony as a fresh Draft-tier decision.

  Art: cauldron_suush_{north,east,south} — QUEUED and VALIDATED (pass) before
  this build started (infrastructure/artpipe/done/, registry.jsonl), deployed
  unchanged to Textures/Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Suush/ below. West mirrors east
  automatically (Graphic_Multi).

  Franchise-free (Q11a): "Suush" and "the Cauldron" are invented names, so
  this stays RM tier — wired directly into RM_PoisonForest.xml's own
  <wildAnimals>, no Utinni patch layer, no MayRequire.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Suush</defName>
    <label>suush</label>
    <description>A translucent globe drifting a few feet off the ground, lit faintly from within by whatever it has most recently digested. A curtain of long, fine gathering tentacles hangs beneath it, combing the roiling gas for the chemistry it lives on. It never comes down, never attacks, and never seems to notice you. It is also, entirely, a bag of the same volatile vapor the Cauldron breathes -- and pays no mind at all to what happens if something punctures it.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>1.6</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>18</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.6</Flammability>
      <MeatAmount>0</MeatAmount>
      <LeatherAmount>0</LeatherAmount>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Wildness>0.5</Wildness>
      <MaxFlightTime>600</MaxFlightTime>
      <FlightCooldown>1</FlightCooldown>
    </statBases>
    <race>
      <body>Bird</body>
      <bloodDef>Filth_Slime</bloodDef>
      <baseBodySize>1.3</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.8</baseHealthScale>
      <foodType>None</foodType>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <lifeExpectancy>12</lifeExpectancy>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <flightStartChanceOnJobStart>1.0</flightStartChanceOnJobStart>
      <canFlyIntoMap>true</canFlyIntoMap>
      <canLeaveMapFlying>false</canLeaveMapFlying>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.3</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.6</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
    </race>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Explosive">
        <explosiveRadius>2.9</explosiveRadius>
        <startWickOnDamageTaken>
          <li>Bullet</li>
          <li>Bomb</li>
        </startWickOnDamageTaken>
        <chanceToStartFire>0.5</chanceToStartFire>
        <postExplosionGasType>ToxGas</postExplosionGasType>
        <explodeOnKilled>true</explodeOnKilled>
        <drawWick>true</drawWick>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalUncommon</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

