  <!--
    CAULDRON_RULED_CONTENT_1 (2026-09-29): the three ruled natives below.
    Text and frames from design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/
    cauldron_bedazzle_cast_2026-09-28.md section 3. All three are invented
    names, so they live in this RM tier and are wired inline in
    RM_PoisonForest.xml (Q11a). One home each (the Cauldron only).
    Art: Textures/Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_<Name>/ (south/east/north, Graphic_Multi).

    RM_Vexxiss: NO CompProperties_Explosive and no explosion of any kind (owner
    ruling, "too many exploding giant beasts"): the Suush comp above is
    deliberately NOT copied. Shearing yields RM_Vexxith through vanilla
    CompProperties_Shearable, which works on a LIVING TAMED animal only
    (CompShearable needs a faction); a corpse yields nothing of it. Wild-vexxiss
    shearing, vent inhaling and gas-tap prying are BEHAVIOURS still owed by
    CAULDRON_MECHANICS_BUILD_1 (vent inhaling and prying need the part-3 vent
    and scaffold defs first). The fire-warden attack and the water-poisoning
    touch are built: RimMandrake.PoisonForest.RM_CompVexxissBehaviour
    (Source/RM_CompVexxissBehaviour.cs), with giveNonToolUserBeatFireVerb so
    the animal owns vanilla's beat-fire verb. Both are Mod Settings toggles.

    RM_Zisska: mineral-rasper. foodType is VegetarianRoughAnimal, so in the
    game it eats plants (vein moss, the crust film, is the nearest thing to
    what the description says). The rasp-stone-off-rock behaviour is a
    follow-on. Meat is the owner-ruled toxic prized meat, RM_ZisskaMeat
    (Defs/ThingDefs_Items), plus a trace of steel as the concentrated metal.

    RM_Eskith: ground bird-adjacent, no flight stats (a drummer, not a flier).
    Its silence-before-a-vent-bloom tell is behaviour: CAULDRON_MECHANICS_BUILD_1.
  -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Vexxiss</defName>
    <label>vexxiss</label>
    <description>The ground here talks all day -- rush and groan and gurgle, the slow engine of the forest's chemistry -- and the vexxiss is the one thing that walks like it belongs in the machine. A hill of slag that moves: plates of smelter-scab and old bark grown together, crystal fans standing down the spine like vents on a boiler, no eyes anywhere on it because it has never needed to see anything. It drinks the ground's breath straight from the wellheads, it hates fire the way a lung hates smoke, and the crews that shear its plates say the trick is not the climbing. The trick is doing it without warming the shears.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>1.4</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>3000</Mass>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <MeatAmount>900</MeatAmount>
      <LeatherAmount>0</LeatherAmount>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.9</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.6</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>2.0</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Wildness>0.95</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>front leg</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>26</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.8</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLegs</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>head</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>22</power>
        <cooldownTime>3</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>true</ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>
        <chanceFactor>0.2</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithHooves</body>
      <bloodDef>Filth_Slime</bloodDef>
      <baseBodySize>6.0</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>8.0</baseHealthScale>
      <foodType>OmnivoreAnimal</foodType>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <lifeExpectancy>80</lifeExpectancy>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0.5</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0.05</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <giveNonToolUserBeatFireVerb>true</giveNonToolUserBeatFireVerb>  <!-- fire warden: owns vanilla's beat-fire verb -->
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>1.5</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>4</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
    </race>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Shearable">
        <shearIntervalDays>60</shearIntervalDays>
        <woolAmount>12</woolAmount>
        <woolDef>RM_Vexxith</woolDef>
      </li>
      <!-- CAULDRON_MECHANICS_BUILD_1 part 5: fire warden + poisons water on touch.
           Radii/intervals are INVENTED tuning. Swap targets are vanilla's own
           toxic-water terrains (Odyssey's toxic-lake set). -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.PoisonForest.RM_CompProperties_VexxissBehaviour">
        <fireScanRadius>14</fireScanRadius>
        <igniterChaseRadius>30</igniterChaseRadius>
        <waterPoisonRadius>1.5</waterPoisonRadius>
        <waterSwaps>
          <li><from>WaterShallow</from><to>ToxicWaterShallow</to></li>
          <li><from>WaterDeep</from><to>ToxicWaterDeep</to></li>
          <li><from>WaterMovingShallow</from><to>ToxicWaterMovingShallow</to></li>
          <li><from>WaterMovingChestDeep</from><to>ToxicWaterMovingChestDeep</to></li>
          <li><from>WaterOceanShallow</from><to>ToxicWaterOceanShallow</to></li>
          <li><from>WaterOceanDeep</from><to>ToxicWaterOceanDeep</to></li>
        </waterSwaps>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalExotic</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

